{
  "requirement": "`CriterionVersion::new` constructs a {term}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.check_version`\nfrom the supplied string. It panics on `\"*\"`, which is reserved for unversioned\nlegacy evidence. When reading a saved version, use `from_recorded` to interpret\n`\"*\"` as `None` and any other string as `Some(version)`.\n`as_str()` borrows the original string. Compare this version with the optional\nversion from a saved record using\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.checking_records.version_match`.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub struct CriterionVersion(/* private fields */);\n\nimpl CriterionVersion {\n    pub fn new(value: impl Into<String>) -> Self;\n    pub fn from_recorded(value: impl Into<String>) -> Option<Self>;\n    pub fn as_str(&self) -> &str;\n    pub fn is_compatible_with(&self, saved: Option<&Self>) -> bool;\n}\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl Clone for CriterionVersion;\nimpl Debug for CriterionVersion;\nimpl<'de> Deserialize<'de> for CriterionVersion;\nimpl Serialize for CriterionVersion;\nimpl PartialEq for CriterionVersion;\nimpl Eq for CriterionVersion;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "Obligations and the tests that cover them:\n\n- `new` panics on `\"*\"`: `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[concrete_criterion_version_rejects_the_legacy_marker]` calls `CriterionVersion::new(\"*\")` under `should_panic` with the expected message.\n- `from_recorded` maps `\"*\"` to `None` and any other string to `Some`:\n  - `wildcard_versions_still_check_inputs_and_errors` asserts `from_recorded(\"*\").is_none()`.\n  - It also decodes `\"v41\"`, `\"v42\"`, `\"V42\"`, `\"v*\"` and `\"\"` as `Some`. The comparison table would fail if any of them decoded to `None`.\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/storage.rs#fn[record_preserves_the_stored_version_encoding]` asserts that `\"review-v1\"` gives `Some(\"review-v1\")` and `\"*\"` gives `None`.\n- `as_str()` borrows the original string: the storage test asserts `as_str` returns `\"review-v1\"` unchanged. `new` delegates to `from_recorded`, so one construction path covers both. I read the implementation only to confirm this.\n- Serialization (listed trait impls): the storage test checks that deserializing `\"*\"` as a `CriterionVersion` errors. It also checks that the wire form round-trips, with `\"*\"` re-emitted for `None`.\n- `is_compatible_with` and the cited `requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.checking_records.version_match`:\n  - `wildcard_versions_still_check_inputs_and_errors` covers a saved `None` passing.\n  - It also covers an exact match, a different version, a prefix (`v42` vs `v420`), a case difference, `v*` against `v42` (no match), and `v*` against `v*` (match).\n  - It exercises both the `Record::is_current` path and a direct `is_compatible_with` call.\n- `Clone`, `Debug`, `PartialEq` and `Eq` are plain derived traits, so they have no conditional or custom logic that needs its own test. Equality is exercised through the match cases above.\n\nI found no obligation without a test, and no wrong expected result. The `public_exports_match_the_appendix` test only checks the exported inventory.",
  "references": "4dc61feb0058c67eff3e7aa5e922853fda5f03b2214914277d96a80e49b84772",
